    "turn_text": "This episode of Against the Grain is brought to you by National Journal's Elections and Politics Package. You can prepare for all the exciting 2022 midterm elections with National Journal's first comprehensive elections and politics offering. So get all the news, data, and insider analysis you need to stay on top of the races that matter most to you. visit go.nationaljournal.com slash elections dash offer. That's go.nationaljournal.com slash elections dash offer. live from my home office. Welcome to the Against the Grain podcast. I'm Josh Kraushar, politics columnist here at National Journal, and I'm very pleased today to be joined by Democratic Congressman Jake Okencloss, who is from the great state of Massachusetts, representing the fourth district in Massachusetts, covering the Boston suburbs, Newton, a few other towns, but we'll go into it on the podcast. Before being elected to the house, Congressmen, Ockencloss served in the Marines, commanding infantry in Afghanistan. He also later served on the Newton, Massachusetts city council for several terms before being elected to the house. Congressmen, Ockencloss is a member of the transportation and infrastructure committee and as vice chairman of the, there's also vice chairman of the financial services. committee. And fun fact, he's the youngest dad in a Democratic House caucus. Congressman, welcome to the Against the Grain podcast. It's good to be here. So let's start out some broad base question. What are the vibes like for House Democrats these days? Do you feel like you've accomplished a lot in this Congress, the presidents accomplished a lot in the last year and a half? And do you feel the country is headed in the right direction?",
