    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49220.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, again, like what you're describing is sort of a very intra-tribal squabble that is pretty far removed from what I think Democrats are going to be able to win on. I just announced a series of endorsements myself to a number of New England front-liners. And these endorsements went to members of Congress who are campaigning for the kitchen table, not for Twitter. I'm really not that interested in, you know, member on member disputes and feuds. I'm not that interested in Twitter spats. I think when we hear from the American people what they're focused on is lowering costs. And we have got to be sending candidates and members who are laser focused on those issues and do it in a pragmatic way. And who have an economic vision that's not just demand side, not just supply side like Republicans are, but confused both supply and demand policy.",
