    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49220.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "I have a good relationship with most members of the caucus. I speak with Representative Ocasio-Cortez relatively frequently. I speak with other members of the squad relatively frequently. I just actually worked with many of them on amending the Domestic Terrorism Violence Prevention Act to make it more respectful of civil liberties, more cognizant of the abuses of the surveillance state at the federal level. I also just wrote an op-ed with Liz Cheney about Ukraine. I am someone who can work with conservatives and progressives. And I do so in a spirit of curiosity and humility. What can I learn from this interaction? What don't I know? What can we agree on from an orthogonal perspective, unless so from a place of ideological certitude or even worse condescension? I just think Democrats in particular have to be incredibly careful that we do not condescend to our voters. We have become elitist and condescending and voters can sense it, and they really don't like it. And I don't blame them.",
