    "turn_idx": 36,
    "turn_text": "I want to talk policy for a minute. The big discussion on Capitol Hill this week is over gun regulation, gun measures after these horrible mass shootings that have taken place across the country, most notably in Texas. There's a difference going on in the House and the Senate. There's a lot more ambitious legislation being debated right now in the House while it seems like Senate Republicans and Democrats, at least a small group of them, led by Democratic Senator Murphy, Republican Senator John Corning of Texas. They're working on a more modest package in terms of some red flag law incentives, background check expansion, perhaps, for younger Americans. What do you think of the smaller scale package? Is that a compromise? You'd be",
