  {
    "episode_id": 49220,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49220.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "Well, you always want to move the overtant window of debate. Pull it as far as you can in your direction and then find the sweet spot within the window where you can get a deal. And you know who was amazing at this was my predecessor, Broni Frank, who was a strong, strong liberal Democrat and yet was famous for finding compromises with Republicans because he would fight hard. He would push that overtant window as far as he could to the left and then When it could go no further, he would find the deal in the middle of it. And I worry that too few members still have that muscle, but how to do that. So I'm going to pull that over to as far as I can on guns, but I'm definitely going to get the deal that we can get. And Senator Murphy, I know, is as passionate and as as well versed on this issue is anybody in the Senate. I know that what he would most want is an assault weapons ban, but I also know that he's a negotiator and he is going to get the best deal he can possibly get, and I support that.",
