    "turn_idx": 63,
    "turn_text": "I here's my biggest fear. My biggest fear is that they. They constitutionally steal it. And what I mean by that is that. Again, the Constitution basically says the states send the electors to Congress and Congress just opens up the envelopes. I mean, there are literally envelopes that they mail to us and we open them up and record them. And what I'm terrified of is that in states like Pennsylvania or Arizona or elsewhere that the margins are narrow enough and the officials are callous and partisan enough that they take close elections and the state legislature or some other body, more likely the state legislature cast the electors towards the MAGA candidate, even though the popular vote was not with the MAGA candidate. And then Congress is stuck in this position of being sent a slate of electors that were certified by the state, which is the only constitutional requirement that we have. And we have to decide are we going to record and tabulate these? Or are we going to ask for an alternative slate of electors? Well, here's the problem. In 2020, it was Democrats saying you cannot do alternative slates of electors. That's unconstitutional. In 2024, we may be in a position where we know that it was stolen at the state level. And we're trying to explain why actually we do need an alternative slate of electors. And it's going to seem very dissonant to the American public. That terrifies me that scenario.",
